# `--founding-file` takes exactly what `adr new --body-file` takes: a MADR
# body (the '## ' sections). init seeds it verbatim as the single founding
# ADR, ADR-0001 (milestone #4 — the pre-v0.2 one-ADR-per-'## '-heading
# grammar is gone). A '## Rules' section in the body makes the founding ADR
# rule-bearing (its rules project into constitution.md); under the default
# sourceTracking.type (none) it carries no source field (plan §2.8).

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

exec constitution init --founding-file founding.md --target claude
stdout 'created .*ADR-0001-founding-constitution\.md'

! grep 'source:' constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md
grep 'Every change ships with tests, no exceptions.' constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md

# the body's '## Rules' section makes ADR-0001 rule-bearing -> its rule
# projects under the rule's slug heading.
grep '## Rules' constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md
grep '#### tests-required' constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md
grep 'Every change ships with tests.' constitution/constitution.md
grep '### tests-required' constitution/constitution.md

exec constitution guard
stdout 'clean'

-- founding.md --
## Context and Problem Statement

Established at project bootstrap by `constitution init`.

## Considered Options

- Adopt this founding decision
- Leave the convention implicit

## Decision Outcome

Every change ships with tests, no exceptions.

## Rules

### testing

#### tests-required
Every change ships with tests.
